<spell-notebook "search examples">
	<header level="1">
		Search
		<header>A search module allows a user to query for results from a selection of data.</>
	</>
	<search-tab-bar showing="examples"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#types">Types</>
				<ui-item link="#states">States</>
				<ui-item link="#variations">Variations</>
				<ui-item link="#more-examples">More Examples</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!--
		EXAMPLES:  Fomantic's search page, its Definition tab section by section (Types, States, Variations), then its
		Examples tab (More Examples).  `source` is a JS PROPERTY;  plain HTML may also write it as a JSON attribute
		(single-quoted), as these examples do, so they need no script.  Fomantic's remote GitHub searches run on a local
		`source` here:  the site never calls a third-party API.  Type in a search to see its results.
	-->
	<section label="Types">
		<!-- GAP I37:  Fomantic's bare prompt (no icon);  ours always draws the search icon. -->
		<section label="Standard" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can display a set of results.">
				<html>
					<ui-search placeholder="Github Repositories..." source="/components/ui/\[%7B%22title%22:%22Fomantic-UI%22,%22description%22:%22Fomantic%20empowers%20designers%20and%20developers%20by%20creating%20a%20shared%20vocabulary%20for%20UI.%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22Fomantic-UI-Docs%22,%22description%22:%22Docs%20for%20Fomantic-UI%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22Fomantic-UI-CSS%22,%22description%22:%22CSS%20only%20distribution%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22Fomantic-UI-LESS%22,%22description%22:%22LESS%20only%20distribution%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22create-fomantic-icons%22,%22description%22:%22Create%20Fomantic%20icons%20from%20Font%20Awesome%22%7D]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
			<example>
				<html>
					<ui-message slot="description" state="info" size="small">Every <code>&lt;ui-search&gt;</code> is drawn as Fomantic's <code>ui icon input</code>, so the icon input needs no extra markup. The <code>icon</code> slot swaps the magnifying glass.</ui-message>
					<ui-search placeholder="Github Repositories..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-Docs\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-CSS\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-LESS\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<!-- GAP I38:  no `clearable` remove icon;  Escape clears the text instead. -->
		<section label="Clearable" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">A search can show a remove icon to be able to cancel a previous search term.</p>
				</html>
				<message slot="description" size="small">Not yet: there is no remove icon. Escape closes the results, and a second Escape clears the text.</message>
				<html>
					<ui-search placeholder="Github Repositories..." value="fomantic" source="\[{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-Docs\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-CSS\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-LESS\"}]">
						<ui-icon slot="icon" name="github"></ui-icon>
					</ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Category" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can display results ordered by categories:  `category`, with each result's `category`.">
				<html>
					<ui-search category placeholder="Search people..." source="\[{\"category\":\"Designers\",\"title\":\"Elliot Fu\",\"description\":\"Film buff\"},{\"category\":\"Designers\",\"title\":\"Helen Troy\",\"description\":\"Wizard\"},{\"category\":\"Developers\",\"title\":\"Jenny Hess\",\"description\":\"Student\"},{\"category\":\"Developers\",\"title\":\"Matt Giampietro\",\"description\":\"Coach\"},{\"category\":\"Writers\",\"title\":\"Stevie Feliciano\",\"description\":\"Library\"},{\"category\":\"Writers\",\"title\":\"Christian Rocha\",\"description\":\"Mixologist\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Horizontal Category" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="You can also display horizontal category names on top of each results instead:  `direction=\"horizontal\"`.">
				<html>
					<ui-search category direction="horizontal" placeholder="Search people..." source="\[{\"category\":\"Designers\",\"title\":\"Elliot Fu\",\"description\":\"Film buff\"},{\"category\":\"Designers\",\"title\":\"Helen Troy\",\"description\":\"Wizard\"},{\"category\":\"Developers\",\"title\":\"Jenny Hess\",\"description\":\"Student\"},{\"category\":\"Developers\",\"title\":\"Matt Giampietro\",\"description\":\"Coach\"},{\"category\":\"Writers\",\"title\":\"Stevie Feliciano\",\"description\":\"Library\"},{\"category\":\"Writers\",\"title\":\"Christian Rocha\",\"description\":\"Mixologist\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Local Search" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">A search can look for results inside a static local source.</p>
					<ui-message slot="description" state="info" size="small">Results that begin with the query come first, then content that matches the query anywhere inside. To match word starts only, set <code>full-text-search="prefix"</code> (Fomantic's <code>fullTextSearch: false</code>).</ui-message>
					<ui-search placeholder="Search countries..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Andorra\"},{\"title\":\"United Arab Emirates\"},{\"title\":\"Afghanistan\"},{\"title\":\"Antigua\"},{\"title\":\"Anguilla\"},{\"title\":\"Albania\"},{\"title\":\"Armenia\"},{\"title\":\"Netherlands Antilles\"},{\"title\":\"Angola\"},{\"title\":\"Argentina\"},{\"title\":\"American Samoa\"},{\"title\":\"Austria\"},{\"title\":\"Australia\"},{\"title\":\"Aruba\"},{\"title\":\"Aland Islands\"},{\"title\":\"Azerbaijan\"},{\"title\":\"Bosnia\"},{\"title\":\"Barbados\"},{\"title\":\"Bangladesh\"},{\"title\":\"Belgium\"},{\"title\":\"Burkina Faso\"},{\"title\":\"Bulgaria\"},{\"title\":\"Bahrain\"},{\"title\":\"Burundi\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Local Category Search" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can look for category results inside a static local source:  `category`, with each result's `category`.">
				<html>
					<ui-search category placeholder="Search countries..." source="\[{\"category\":\"South America\",\"title\":\"Brazil\"},{\"category\":\"South America\",\"title\":\"Peru\"},{\"category\":\"North America\",\"title\":\"Canada\"},{\"category\":\"Asia\",\"title\":\"South Korea\"},{\"category\":\"Asia\",\"title\":\"Japan\"},{\"category\":\"Asia\",\"title\":\"China\"},{\"category\":\"Europe\",\"title\":\"Denmark\"},{\"category\":\"Europe\",\"title\":\"England\"},{\"category\":\"Europe\",\"title\":\"France\"},{\"category\":\"Europe\",\"title\":\"Germany\"},{\"category\":\"Africa\",\"title\":\"Ethiopia\"},{\"category\":\"Africa\",\"title\":\"Nigeria\"},{\"category\":\"Africa\",\"title\":\"Zimbabwe\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Search ignoring Diacritics" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search field can allow a user to ignore all diacritics while searching:  `ignore-diacritics`, so `a` matches `á`.">
				<html>
					<ui-search ignore-diacritics full-text-search="exact" placeholder="Search Diacritics..." source="\[{\"title\":\"André\"},{\"title\":\"Bokmål\"},{\"title\":\"café\"},{\"title\":\"cafetería\"},{\"title\":\"château\"},{\"title\":\"décolleté\"},{\"title\":\"Élysée\"},{\"title\":\"Fräulein\"},{\"title\":\"garçon\"},{\"title\":\"háček\"},{\"title\":\"inrō\"},{\"title\":\"jūjutsu\"},{\"title\":\"kroužek\"},{\"title\":\"La Niña\"},{\"title\":\"Māori\"},{\"title\":\"négligée\"},{\"title\":\"pączki\"},{\"title\":\"Québec\"},{\"title\":\"ragoût\"},{\"title\":\"Škoda\"},{\"title\":\"takahē\"},{\"title\":\"über\"},{\"title\":\"voilà\"},{\"title\":\"whekī\"},{\"title\":\"c Zoë\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Highlight search matches" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search field can highlight matching strings inside the search results:  `highlight-matches`.">
				<html>
					<ui-search highlight-matches placeholder="Search..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Andorra\"},{\"title\":\"United Arab Emirates\"},{\"title\":\"Afghanistan\"},{\"title\":\"Antigua\"},{\"title\":\"Anguilla\"},{\"title\":\"Albania\"},{\"title\":\"Armenia\"},{\"title\":\"Netherlands Antilles\"},{\"title\":\"Angola\"},{\"title\":\"Argentina\"},{\"title\":\"American Samoa\"},{\"title\":\"Austria\"},{\"title\":\"Australia\"},{\"title\":\"Aruba\"},{\"title\":\"Aland Islands\"},{\"title\":\"Azerbaijan\"},{\"title\":\"Bosnia\"},{\"title\":\"Barbados\"},{\"title\":\"Bangladesh\"},{\"title\":\"Belgium\"},{\"title\":\"Burkina Faso\"},{\"title\":\"Bulgaria\"},{\"title\":\"Bahrain\"},{\"title\":\"Burundi\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Descriptions, prices and links" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A result can carry a `description`, a `price`, an `image` and a `url`:  choosing a result with a `url` follows it.">
				<html>
					<ui-search highlight-matches placeholder="Search fruit..." source="/components/ui/\[%7B%22title%22:%22Apple%22,%22description%22:%22Crisp%20and%20sweet%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22Apricot%22,%22description%22:%22Soft,%20from%20Valencia%22,%22price%22:%22$2.00%22%7D,%7B%22title%22:%22Grape%22,%22url%22:%22"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="States">
		<!-- GAP I39:  Fomantic's second and third rows (`blue loading double`, `slow elastic pink loading`) have no attribute value. -->
		<section label="Loading" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can show a loading indicator.  It also spins while a remote query runs.">
				<search loading placeholder="Search..."/>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Variations">
		<section label="Disabled" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can show it is currently unable to be interacted with:  it's dimmed and left out of the form.">
				<search disabled category placeholder="Search animals..."/>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Scrolling" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">A search can have its results scroll.</p>
					<ui-message slot="description" state="info" size="small">The scroll height depends on the viewport: 4 results' height, 6 / 8 / 12 from 768px / 992px / 1920px. <code>--ui-search-results-max-height</code> replaces it at every width.</ui-message>
					<ui-message slot="description" size="small">Add <code>resizable</code> to <code>scrolling</code> and a native resize handle appears at the bottom right of the results.</ui-message>
					<ui-search scrolling max-results="0" placeholder="Search countries..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Andorra\"},{\"title\":\"United Arab Emirates\"},{\"title\":\"Afghanistan\"},{\"title\":\"Antigua\"},{\"title\":\"Anguilla\"},{\"title\":\"Albania\"},{\"title\":\"Armenia\"},{\"title\":\"Netherlands Antilles\"},{\"title\":\"Angola\"},{\"title\":\"Argentina\"},{\"title\":\"American Samoa\"},{\"title\":\"Austria\"},{\"title\":\"Australia\"},{\"title\":\"Aruba\"},{\"title\":\"Aland Islands\"},{\"title\":\"Azerbaijan\"},{\"title\":\"Bosnia\"},{\"title\":\"Barbados\"},{\"title\":\"Bangladesh\"},{\"title\":\"Belgium\"},{\"title\":\"Burkina Faso\"},{\"title\":\"Bulgaria\"},{\"title\":\"Bahrain\"},{\"title\":\"Burundi\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Height" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">A search can be <code>very-short</code> (0.75x of the default height) so that more results can be glanced. Or it can be short, long (2x) or very-long.</p>
				</html>
				<message slot="description" state="info" size="small">The default height is the height of one result times the number of results shown at the current breakpoint.</message>
				<html>
					<ui-search length="very-short" max-results="0" placeholder="Search countries..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Andorra\"},{\"title\":\"United Arab Emirates\"},{\"title\":\"Afghanistan\"},{\"title\":\"Antigua\"},{\"title\":\"Anguilla\"},{\"title\":\"Albania\"},{\"title\":\"Armenia\"},{\"title\":\"Netherlands Antilles\"},{\"title\":\"Angola\"},{\"title\":\"Argentina\"},{\"title\":\"American Samoa\"},{\"title\":\"Austria\"},{\"title\":\"Australia\"},{\"title\":\"Aruba\"},{\"title\":\"Aland Islands\"},{\"title\":\"Azerbaijan\"},{\"title\":\"Bosnia\"},{\"title\":\"Barbados\"},{\"title\":\"Bangladesh\"},{\"title\":\"Belgium\"},{\"title\":\"Burkina Faso\"},{\"title\":\"Bulgaria\"},{\"title\":\"Bahrain\"},{\"title\":\"Burundi\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
			<example description="Long:  2x of the default height.">
				<html>
					<ui-search length="long" max-results="0" placeholder="Search countries..." source="\[{\"title\":\"Andorra\"},{\"title\":\"United Arab Emirates\"},{\"title\":\"Afghanistan\"},{\"title\":\"Antigua\"},{\"title\":\"Anguilla\"},{\"title\":\"Albania\"},{\"title\":\"Armenia\"},{\"title\":\"Netherlands Antilles\"},{\"title\":\"Angola\"},{\"title\":\"Argentina\"},{\"title\":\"American Samoa\"},{\"title\":\"Austria\"},{\"title\":\"Australia\"},{\"title\":\"Aruba\"},{\"title\":\"Aland Islands\"},{\"title\":\"Azerbaijan\"},{\"title\":\"Bosnia\"},{\"title\":\"Barbados\"},{\"title\":\"Bangladesh\"},{\"title\":\"Belgium\"},{\"title\":\"Burkina Faso\"},{\"title\":\"Bulgaria\"},{\"title\":\"Bahrain\"},{\"title\":\"Burundi\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Fluid" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can have its results take up the width of its container.">
				<html>
					<ui-search fluid category placeholder="Search animals..." source="\[{\"category\":\"Mammals\",\"title\":\"Cat\"},{\"category\":\"Mammals\",\"title\":\"Dog\"},{\"category\":\"Birds\",\"title\":\"Crow\"},{\"category\":\"Birds\",\"title\":\"Owl\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<section label="Aligned" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can have its results aligned to its left or right container edge:  `align=\"right\"` extends them to the left.">
				<html>
					<ui-search align="right" category placeholder="Search animals..." source="\[{\"category\":\"Mammals\",\"title\":\"Cat\",\"description\":\"Aligned to the right edge\"},{\"category\":\"Mammals\",\"title\":\"Dog\"},{\"category\":\"Birds\",\"title\":\"Crow\"},{\"category\":\"Birds\",\"title\":\"Owl\"}]"></ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<!-- GAP I37:  Fomantic's sizes are bare prompts;  ours keep the search icon. -->
		<section label="Size" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="A search can vary in size.">
				<search size="mini" placeholder="Mini search..."/>
				<search size="tiny" placeholder="Tiny search..."/>
				<search size="small" placeholder="Small search..."/>
				<search size="large" placeholder="Large search..."/>
				<search size="big" placeholder="Big search..."/>
				<search size="huge" placeholder="Huge search..."/>
				<search size="massive" placeholder="Massive search..."/>
			</example>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="More Examples">
		<!-- GAP I37, I40:  no left icon input;  no response field mapping, so the GitHub search is a local source. -->
		<section label="Using Different Response Fields" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example description="Fomantic maps a server's answer to its result fields with `fields`;  a remote `<ui-search url>` expects Fomantic's own answer shape instead (`{ results: \[...] }`, or `{ results: { name: { name, results } } }` by category). Shape a third-party API on your server, or set `source` from a `ui-search` listener:  here, a local source.">
				<html>
					<ui-search min-characters="3" placeholder="Search GitHub" source="\[{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI\",\"url\":\"#fomantic-ui\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-Docs\",\"url\":\"#fomantic-ui-docs\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-CSS\",\"url\":\"#fomantic-ui-css\"},{\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-LESS\",\"url\":\"#fomantic-ui-less\"}]">
						<ui-icon slot="icon" name="github"></ui-icon>
					</ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>

		<!-- GAP I40:  no `onResponse` hook to regroup a third-party answer. -->
		<section label="Using API Settings" sticky collapsible dividing>
			<example>
				<html>
					<p slot="description">Fomantic's <code>apiSettings.onResponse</code> regroups GitHub's answer by language. Ours: a <code>category</code> search over results that carry a <code>category</code>, here a local source.</p>
				</html>
				<message slot="description" state="warning" size="small" heading="Be careful with foreign remote API services">Results are rendered as TEXT, never HTML, so a hostile title or description can't inject markup.</message>
				<html>
					<ui-search category min-characters="3" placeholder="Search GitHub" source="\[{\"category\":\"JavaScript\",\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI\",\"description\":\"A shared vocabulary for UI\"},{\"category\":\"JavaScript\",\"title\":\"create-fomantic-icons\",\"description\":\"Create Fomantic icons from Font Awesome\"},{\"category\":\"CSS\",\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-CSS\",\"description\":\"CSS only distribution\"},{\"category\":\"Less\",\"title\":\"Fomantic-UI-LESS\",\"description\":\"LESS only distribution\"}]">
						<ui-icon slot="icon" name="github"></ui-icon>
					</ui-search>
				</html>
			</example>
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
